              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Trichiasis—normal hair from the skin contacting corneal or conjunctival surface.",
              "pdf_page": 564,
              "printed_page": 482,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Distichiasis—abnormal hairs that emerge from the meibomian glands along the eyelid margin; may contact corneal or conjunctival",
              "pdf_page": 564,
              "printed_page": 482,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "surface.",
              "pdf_page": 564,
              "printed_page": 482,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Ectopic cilia—abnormal hairs that emerge through the palpebral conjunctiva several millimeters from the lid margin; contact the corneal surface.",
              "pdf_page": 564,
              "printed_page": 482,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
